<article class="env-lemma" id="0AEJ">
       
      
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0AEJ">Lemma <span data-tag="0AEJ">76.35.3</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ X \ar[rr]_ h \ar[rd]_ f &  &  Y \ar[ld]^ g \\  &  B }  \]
</div>
  <p> be a commutative diagram of morphism of algebraic spaces over $S$. Let $b \in B$ and let $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(k) \to B$ be a morphism in the equivalence class of $b$. Assume </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$X \to B$ is a proper morphism, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$Y \to B$ is separated and locally of finite type, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
one of the following is true 
</p>
<ol>
  <li><p>
the image of $|X_ k| \to |Y_ k|$ is finite, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
the image of $|f|^{-1}(\{ b\} )$ in $|Y|$ is finite and $B$ is decent. 
</p>
</li>
</ol>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> Then there is an open subspace $B' \subset B$ containing $b$ such that $X_{B'} \to Y_{B'}$ factors through a closed subspace $Z \subset Y_{B'}$ finite over $B'$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $Z \subset Y$ be the scheme theoretic image of $h$, see Morphisms of Spaces, Section <a href="/tag/082W" data-tag="082W">67.16</a>. By Morphisms of Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/0AGD" data-tag="0AGD">67.40.8</a> the morphism $X \to Z$ is surjective and $Z \to B$ is proper. Thus 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \{ x \in |X|\text{ lying over }b\}  \to \{ z \in |Z|\text{ lying over }b\}   \]
</div>
    <p>
       and $|X_ k| \to |Z_ k|$ are surjective. We see that either (3)(a) or (3)(b) imply that $Z \to B$ is quasi-finite all points of $|Z|$ lying over $b$ by Decent Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/0ACK" data-tag="0ACK">68.18.10</a>. Hence $Z \to B$ is finite in an open neighbourhood of $b$ by Lemma <a href="/tag/0A4Y" data-tag="0A4Y">76.35.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>